From aac4d1344878d830653cfc024de8a8abd43fb538 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment archive <experiment@invalid.example>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 18:35:54 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] pstore: preserve native records when backend erase fails

Do not unlink the exported record when its backend refuses erasure.
This native 3.18 prerequisite preserves the existing missing-callback
refusal and does not implement backing-store ownership.

Host tests exercise the exact inode and ramoops function bodies with
injected storage and erase refusal. No full kernel build or hardware
test has been performed. The archive identity is synthetic and
non-certifying; not submission-ready.
---
 fs/pstore/inode.c | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/pstore/inode.c b/fs/pstore/inode.c
index 77bdcdc..e5adde8 100644
--- a/fs/pstore/inode.c
+++ b/fs/pstore/inode.c
@@ -175,12 +175,16 @@ static int pstore_unlink(struct inode *dir, struct dentry *dentry)
 {
 	struct pstore_private *p = dentry->d_inode->i_private;
 
-	if (p->psi->erase)
-		p->psi->erase(p->type, p->id, p->count,
-			      dentry->d_inode->i_ctime, p->psi);
-	else
+	int ret;
+
+	if (!p->psi->erase)
 		return -EPERM;
 
+	ret = p->psi->erase(p->type, p->id, p->count,
+			    dentry->d_inode->i_ctime, p->psi);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
 	return simple_unlink(dir, dentry);
 }
 
